 initial sync. The final token/config swap is serialized behind any active sync, so an older request
 cannot restore superseded authorization.
 
+If the matching previous installation is rejected with HTTP 401 or 403, `connect` reconciles that
+revoked authorization under the lifecycle lock, removes the stale local token and automatic state,
+and starts a fresh pairing without requiring `disconnect` or an abandoned pairing. The installation
+identity, local source IDs, and discovered source roots remain local and stable. Incomplete auxiliary
+cleanup is reported as a warning; other reconciliation errors, including transient server or network
+failures, leave the previous valid connection in place and do not start replacement pairing.
+
